{
    "background_story": "Uriel was a member of the ancient nobility, known for his vast landholdings and wise stewardship. His family had owned the rolling hills and fertile valleys of Ashwood for generations, and Uriel took great pride in managing the estate. He was a just and fair lord, beloved by his tenants and villagers, who appreciated his commitment to the land and its people. Under his leadership, Ashwood flourished, becoming a model of sustainable agriculture and innovative farming practices. Uriel's landholdings were not just a source of wealth, but a symbol of his family's legacy and his own sense of responsibility to the community. He worked tirelessly to preserve the natural beauty of the land, ensuring that Ashwood remained a thriving and prosperous domain for generations to come.",
